sequenceDiagram
    participant Pri as Primary
    participant WAL as WAL stream
    participant SP as Startup (heap2_redo)
    participant RC as ResolveRecoveryConflictWithSnapshot
    participant PA as procarray
    participant Bk as Standby backend (long SELECT)
    participant Cancel as Cancel timeout

    Note over Pri: VACUUM marks tuples xmin<800 as dead
    Pri->>WAL: XLOG_HEAP2_PRUNE_VACUUM_SCAN<br/>(snapshotConflictHorizon=800)
    WAL->>SP: heap2_redo dispatch
    SP->>SP: extract horizon=800 from record
    SP->>RC: ResolveRecoveryConflictWithSnapshot(800, rnode)
    RC->>PA: GetConflictingVirtualXIDs(horizon=800)
    PA-->>RC: [vxid_B] (B's xmin=500 < 800)
    RC->>Bk: SendProcSignal(vxid_B,<br/>PROCSIG_RECOVERY_CONFLICT_SNAPSHOT)
    Bk->>Bk: HandleRecoveryConflictInterrupt:<br/>RecoveryConflictPending=true<br/>Reasons[SNAPSHOT]=true<br/>InterruptPending=true
    activate Cancel
    Cancel->>Cancel: sleep up to<br/>max_standby_streaming_delay
    deactivate Cancel
    alt Backend hits CFI in time
        Bk->>Bk: ProcessRecoveryConflictInterrupt
        Bk->>Bk: ereport(ERROR,<br/>"canceling statement due to<br/>conflict with recovery")
        Bk-->>RC: VXID released
    else Timeout fires
        RC->>Bk: CancelVirtualTransaction(vxid_B,<br/>PROCSIG_RECOVERY_CONFLICT_SNAPSHOT)
        Bk->>Bk: next CFI: ERROR
    end
    RC-->>SP: return (no more conflicting VXIDs)
    SP->>SP: XLogReadBufferForRedoExtended cleanup-lock OK
    SP->>SP: apply prune to heap page
    SP->>SP: PageSetLSN; MarkBufferDirty
